  <article class="tp-article">

  <div class="tp-answer" id="quick-answer"><p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> VO2 max is the most oxygen your body can use per minute, in ml per kg of body weight. For a man in his 30s, about <strong>44 is good and 48+ excellent</strong>; for a woman in her 30s, about <strong>38 is good and 42+ excellent</strong> (Cooper Institute norms).</p></div>

