  <section id="tests" aria-labelledby="tests-h">
    <h2 id="tests-h">The Four Tests and Their Formulas</h2>
    <ul class="tp-steps" style="list-style:disc"><li><strong>Resting heart rate (Uth):</strong> VO2 max &asymp; 15.3 &times; max HR &divide; resting HR. No exercise needed; least precise.</li>
      <li><strong>Cooper 12-minute run:</strong> run as far as you can in 12 minutes on a track. VO2 max = (meters &minus; 504.9) &divide; 44.73.</li>
      <li><strong>1.5-mile run:</strong> run 1.5 miles (2.4 km) as fast as you can. VO2 max = 483 &divide; time in minutes + 3.5.</li>
      <li><strong>Rockport 1-mile walk:</strong> walk 1 mile as fast as you can and take your heart rate at the finish. Suits beginners and older adults.</li></ul><p>Field tests are typically within about 10% of a lab test. Warm up first and only do the running tests if you are already active and healthy.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="improve" aria-labelledby="improve-h">
    <h2 id="improve-h">How to Improve Your VO2 Max</h2>
    <p>VO2 max responds well to training. Most people improve 10&ndash;20% in a few months with a mix of easy aerobic work and one or two weekly interval sessions, such as 4 &times; 4 minutes at 85&ndash;95% of max heart rate with 3 minutes easy between. Use the <a href="/heart-rate-zone-calculator/">heart rate zone calculator</a> to set the intensities. Losing body fat also raises VO2 max per kilogram.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-h">
    <h2 id="faq-h">VO2 Max FAQ</h2>
      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>What is a good VO2 max?</h3></summary><p>It depends on age and sex. For men in their 30s, about 44 ml/kg/min is good and over 48 excellent; for women in their 30s, about 38 is good and over 42 excellent.</p></details>
      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>Can you calculate VO2 max without a test?</h3></summary><p>Roughly. The resting heart rate method (15.3 × max HR ÷ resting HR) needs no exercise, but it is less accurate than a field test such as the Cooper run or Rockport walk.</p></details>
      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>How accurate is my watch’s VO2 max?</h3></summary><p>Many fitness watches estimate VO2 max from pace and heart rate during runs and are often within about 5% for runners, but they can be further off for other activities or with poor heart rate data.</p></details>
      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>What is the VO2 max of elite athletes?</h3></summary><p>Elite male endurance athletes often measure 70–85 ml/kg/min and elite women 60–75, compared with about 35–45 for typical adults.</p></details>
      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>Does VO2 max decline with age?</h3></summary><p>Yes, by about 10% per decade after 30 in inactive people, and roughly half that in people who keep training.</p></details>
  </section>

